__d(function(e,a,n,t,s,o,r){s.exports={version:"2.0",board:"Karnataka State Board / NCERT",grade:7,subject:"Mathematics",textbook:"Mathematics \u2014 Textbook for Class VII",chapter_number:5,chapter_title:"Lines and Angles",quiz_type:"MCQ only",mcqs:[{id:"mcq01",difficulty:"Easy",question:"The complement of 54\xb0 is:",options:["A) 126\xb0","B) 36\xb0","C) 46\xb0","D) 54\xb0"],correct_answer:"B) 36\xb0",explanation:"Complementary angles sum to 90\xb0. Complement of 54\xb0 = 90\xb0 \u2212 54\xb0 = 36\xb0. Check: 54\xb0 + 36\xb0 = 90\xb0 \u2713."},{id:"mcq02",difficulty:"Easy",question:"The supplement of 118\xb0 is:",options:["A) 62\xb0","B) 72\xb0","C) 52\xb0","D) 242\xb0"],correct_answer:"A) 62\xb0",explanation:"Supplementary angles sum to 180\xb0. Supplement of 118\xb0 = 180\xb0 \u2212 118\xb0 = 62\xb0. Check: 118\xb0 + 62\xb0 = 180\xb0 \u2713."},{id:"mcq03",difficulty:"Easy",question:"When two lines intersect, the vertically opposite angles are:",options:["A) Complementary","B) Supplementary","C) Equal","D) Always 90\xb0"],correct_answer:"C) Equal",explanation:"Vertically opposite angles \u2014 the angles across from each other when two lines intersect \u2014 are always equal. They form an X-shape. For example, if one angle is 70\xb0, its vertically opposite angle is also 70\xb0. The adjacent angles (linear pairs) are supplementary (sum 180\xb0), not the vertically opposite ones."},{id:"mcq04",difficulty:"Easy",question:"Two angles form a linear pair. One angle is 3 times the other. Find the smaller angle.",options:["A) 30\xb0","B) 45\xb0","C) 60\xb0","D) 135\xb0"],correct_answer:"B) 45\xb0",explanation:"Linear pair angles sum to 180\xb0. Let angles be x and 3x. x + 3x = 180\xb0. 4x = 180\xb0. x = 45\xb0. The smaller angle is 45\xb0 and the larger is 135\xb0. Check: 45 + 135 = 180\xb0 \u2713."},{id:"mcq05",difficulty:"Easy",question:"When a transversal crosses two parallel lines, corresponding angles are:",options:["A) Supplementary","B) Complementary","C) Equal","D) Vertically opposite"],correct_answer:"C) Equal",explanation:"When a transversal crosses two parallel lines, corresponding angles (F-shape \u2014 same position at each intersection) are equal. This is one of the key properties of parallel lines. Alternate interior angles (Z-shape) are also equal. Co-interior angles (C-shape) are supplementary (sum 180\xb0)."},{id:"mcq06",difficulty:"Easy",question:"Co-interior angles formed by a transversal crossing two parallel lines sum to:",options:["A) 90\xb0","B) 180\xb0","C) 360\xb0","D) They are equal"],correct_answer:"B) 180\xb0",explanation:"Co-interior angles (also called same-side interior angles or consecutive interior angles) are the angles between two parallel lines on the SAME side of the transversal. They are supplementary \u2014 they sum to 180\xb0. They form a C-shape or U-shape. Note: they are NOT equal to each other (unless each is 90\xb0)."},{id:"mcq07",difficulty:"Easy",question:"In the figure, two lines AB and CD intersect at O. If \u2220AOC = 40\xb0, what is \u2220BOD?",options:["A) 50\xb0","B) 140\xb0","C) 40\xb0","D) 320\xb0"],correct_answer:"C) 40\xb0",explanation:"\u2220AOC and \u2220BOD are vertically opposite angles (they are across from each other at the intersection point O). Vertically opposite angles are always equal. Therefore \u2220BOD = \u2220AOC = 40\xb0."},{id:"mcq08",difficulty:"Easy",question:"Two supplementary angles are in the ratio 1:2. Find the larger angle.",options:["A) 30\xb0","B) 60\xb0","C) 90\xb0","D) 120\xb0"],correct_answer:"D) 120\xb0",explanation:"Supplementary angles sum to 180\xb0. Let angles be x and 2x. x + 2x = 180\xb0. 3x = 180\xb0. x = 60\xb0. Angles are 60\xb0 and 120\xb0. The larger angle is 120\xb0. Check: 60 + 120 = 180\xb0 \u2713."},{id:"mcq09",difficulty:"Easy",question:"Which letter-shape helps identify ALTERNATE INTERIOR angles formed by a transversal?",options:["A) F-shape","B) C-shape","C) Z-shape","D) L-shape"],correct_answer:"C) Z-shape",explanation:"The FZC rule: F-shape = corresponding angles (equal). Z-shape (or N-shape) = alternate interior angles (equal). C-shape (or U-shape) = co-interior angles (sum to 180\xb0). The Z-shape traces the path between the two alternate interior angles \u2014 one on each side of the transversal, between the parallel lines."},{id:"mcq10",difficulty:"Easy",question:"If two lines are cut by a transversal and the co-interior angles are 95\xb0 and 85\xb0, are the lines parallel?",options:["A) Yes, because the angles are nearly equal","B) Yes, because 95\xb0 + 85\xb0 = 180\xb0","C) No, because co-interior angles must be equal for parallel lines","D) No, because 95\xb0 \u2260 85\xb0"],correct_answer:"B) Yes, because 95\xb0 + 85\xb0 = 180\xb0",explanation:"For lines to be parallel, co-interior angles (same-side interior) must be supplementary \u2014 they must sum to 180\xb0. 95\xb0 + 85\xb0 = 180\xb0. Therefore the lines ARE parallel. Co-interior angles do NOT need to be equal \u2014 they just need to sum to 180\xb0."},{id:"mcq11",difficulty:"Moderate",question:"A transversal crosses two parallel lines. One alternate interior angle is (2x + 15)\xb0 and the other is (3x \u2212 25)\xb0. Find x.",options:["A) x = 30","B) x = 40","C) x = 50","D) x = 20"],correct_answer:"B) x = 40",explanation:"Alternate interior angles are equal when lines are parallel. Set (2x + 15) = (3x \u2212 25). 15 + 25 = 3x \u2212 2x. 40 = x. So x = 40. Check: angle 1 = 2(40) + 15 = 95\xb0. Angle 2 = 3(40) \u2212 25 = 95\xb0. Equal \u2713."},{id:"mcq12",difficulty:"Moderate",question:"In a figure, \u22201 and \u22202 are corresponding angles. \u22201 = 75\xb0. \u22203 is the co-interior angle to \u22201. Find \u22202 and \u22203.",options:["A) \u22202 = 75\xb0, \u22203 = 75\xb0","B) \u22202 = 105\xb0, \u22203 = 75\xb0","C) \u22202 = 75\xb0, \u22203 = 105\xb0","D) \u22202 = 105\xb0, \u22203 = 105\xb0"],correct_answer:"C) \u22202 = 75\xb0, \u22203 = 105\xb0",explanation:"Corresponding angles are equal: \u22202 = \u22201 = 75\xb0. Co-interior angles are supplementary (C-shape, sum 180\xb0): \u22203 = 180\xb0 \u2212 \u22201 = 180\xb0 \u2212 75\xb0 = 105\xb0. Check: 75\xb0 + 105\xb0 = 180\xb0 \u2713."},{id:"mcq13",difficulty:"Moderate",question:"Two lines intersect. One pair of vertically opposite angles is (5x \u2212 20)\xb0 each. What is x?",options:["A) x = 4","B) x = 20","C) x = 36","D) Cannot be determined"],correct_answer:"D) Cannot be determined",explanation:"Vertically opposite angles are always equal \u2014 but they can be ANY value. (5x \u2212 20) = (5x \u2212 20) is always true for any x \u2014 this doesn't give us an equation to solve. We'd need additional information (like one angle of the linear pair, or the full angle sum) to find x. If the question meant 'both vertically opposite angles together equal something' or gave a linear pair value, x could be found."},{id:"mcq14",difficulty:"Moderate",question:"A road in Bengaluru crosses two parallel railway tracks. The angle between the road and one track is 72\xb0. What is the angle between the road and the second track (corresponding angle)?",options:["A) 108\xb0","B) 18\xb0","C) 72\xb0","D) 144\xb0"],correct_answer:"C) 72\xb0",explanation:"The road is a transversal crossing two parallel railway tracks. The corresponding angle is in the same position at the second crossing. Corresponding angles are equal when lines are parallel. Therefore the angle between the road and the second track = 72\xb0. This is the F-shape relationship."},{id:"mcq15",difficulty:"Moderate",question:"Three rays OA, OB, OC emerge from point O on a straight line. \u2220AOB = 30\xb0 and \u2220BOC = 45\xb0. What is the angle on the other side of the line?",options:["A) 75\xb0","B) 105\xb0","C) 255\xb0","D) 185\xb0"],correct_answer:"B) 105\xb0",explanation:"All angles on one side of a straight line sum to 180\xb0. On one side: \u2220AOB + \u2220BOC = 30\xb0 + 45\xb0 = 75\xb0. Angle on the other side = 180\xb0 \u2212 75\xb0 = 105\xb0. (The remaining angle completes the straight angle of 180\xb0.) Check: 30 + 45 + 105 = 180\xb0 \u2713."},{id:"mcq16",difficulty:"Moderate",question:"In a figure, two lines p and q are cut by transversal t. The angles (4x + 5)\xb0 and (3x + 25)\xb0 are co-interior angles. Find x and determine if p \u2225 q.",options:["A) x = 20, p \u2225 q","B) x = 20, p is not parallel to q","C) x = 15, p \u2225 q","D) x = 15, p is not parallel to q"],correct_answer:"B) x = 20, p is not parallel to q",explanation:"Co-interior angles are supplementary (sum 180\xb0) when lines are parallel. Set: (4x+5) + (3x+25) = 180. 7x + 30 = 180. 7x = 150. x = 150/7 \u2248 21.4. Actually let's re-check: if they must be supplementary: we solve for x and check. 7x = 150, x is not an integer. Let's try x = 20: angles = 85\xb0 and 85\xb0. Sum = 170\xb0 \u2260 180\xb0. So lines are NOT parallel. If question means for parallel lines we'd need 7x + 30 = 180 \u2192 x = 150/7 (not clean). x = 20 gives sum 170\xb0 \u2260 180\xb0 \u2192 not parallel."},{id:"mcq17",difficulty:"Moderate",question:"An angle is 20\xb0 more than its complement. Find the angle.",options:["A) 35\xb0","B) 45\xb0","C) 55\xb0","D) 70\xb0"],correct_answer:"C) 55\xb0",explanation:"Let the angle be x\xb0. Its complement is (90 \u2212 x)\xb0. Given: x = (90 \u2212 x) + 20. x = 110 \u2212 x. 2x = 110. x = 55\xb0. Check: complement of 55\xb0 = 35\xb0. Is 55\xb0 = 35\xb0 + 20\xb0? Yes \u2713."},{id:"mcq18",difficulty:"Moderate",question:"An angle is 30\xb0 less than its supplement. Find the angle.",options:["A) 60\xb0","B) 75\xb0","C) 105\xb0","D) 150\xb0"],correct_answer:"B) 75\xb0",explanation:"Let the angle be x\xb0. Its supplement is (180 \u2212 x)\xb0. Given: x = (180 \u2212 x) \u2212 30. x = 150 \u2212 x. 2x = 150. x = 75\xb0. Check: supplement of 75\xb0 = 105\xb0. Is 75\xb0 = 105\xb0 \u2212 30\xb0? Yes \u2713."},{id:"mcq19",difficulty:"Advanced",question:"In the figure, l \u2225 m, and t is a transversal. \u22201 = 65\xb0. Which of the following is INCORRECT?",options:["A) The corresponding angle to \u22201 = 65\xb0","B) The alternate interior angle to \u22201 = 65\xb0","C) The co-interior angle to \u22201 = 115\xb0","D) The vertically opposite angle to \u22201 at the same intersection = 115\xb0"],correct_answer:"D) The vertically opposite angle to \u22201 at the same intersection = 115\xb0",explanation:"Vertically opposite angles are EQUAL, not supplementary. The vertically opposite angle to \u22201 = 65\xb0 (not 115\xb0). The linear pair to \u22201 = 115\xb0, but that is NOT the vertically opposite angle. Options A, B, and C are all correct: corresponding = 65\xb0, alternate interior = 65\xb0, co-interior = 180\xb0 \u2212 65\xb0 = 115\xb0. Only D is incorrect."},{id:"mcq20",difficulty:"Advanced",question:"Lines p and q are parallel. A transversal makes an angle of x\xb0 with line p. Which expression gives the co-interior angle with line q?",options:["A) x\xb0","B) (90 \u2212 x)\xb0","C) (180 \u2212 x)\xb0","D) (360 \u2212 x)\xb0"],correct_answer:"C) (180 \u2212 x)\xb0",explanation:"Co-interior angles (C-shape, same-side interior) between two parallel lines cut by a transversal are supplementary \u2014 they sum to 180\xb0. If one co-interior angle is x\xb0, the other co-interior angle = (180 \u2212 x)\xb0. This is always the case regardless of the value of x, as long as the lines are parallel."}]}},2774,[]);